{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>May YHWH lift His face toward you.</b> He will direct His face toward you to grant you success and to gladden you, like ״ואיך אשא פני אל יואב אחיך״ (how shall I lift my face to Joab your brother), which is interpreted: I will receive his face. And what is written, ״אשר לא ישא פנים״ — who does not lift faces — its meaning is: He has no need to flatter any person who pleads with Him concerning all his transgressions, to set aside His retribution and His justice. Example: ״לולי פני יהושפט אני נושא״ — were it not that I lift the face of Jehoshaphat."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:46.291040158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}